int bc_debug_disable(bc_client_t *c);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Disables the debugger for the current session.
This removes all breakpoints, unregisters the debug pre\-command hook,
and resets the debug state to inactive.
The server sends a confirmation response on \f[CR]CHAN_DEBUG\f[R]
(channel 4).
.PP
After disabling, commands execute at full speed without breakpoint
checking overhead.
The break\-hit callback registered via
\f[CR]bc_debug_on_break_hit()\f[R] is \f[B]not\f[R] removed; it persists
so that re\-enabling the debugger does not require re\-registration.
.PP
Calling \f[CR]bc_debug_disable()\f[R] when the debugger is not enabled
is a no\-op and returns \f[CR]BC_OK\f[R].
.PP
If execution is currently stopped at a breakpoint when
\f[CR]bc_debug_disable()\f[R] is called, execution is resumed
(equivalent to an implicit \f[CR]bc_debug_continue()\f[R]) before the
debugger is disabled.
